description:
Review finding on sutra/276 (high). `src/guard.rs:405 language_from_path` only recognizes `.rs` and `.dart`:

    fn language_from_path(path: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
        if path.ends_with(".rs") { Some("rust") }
        else if path.ends_with(".dart") { Some("dart") }
        else { None }
    }

`parse_proposed` returns `None` for every other extension, so `imports` is empty and `import_pattern` anchors cannot match when writing a new Python/TypeScript/JavaScript/C file. That is sutra/276's headline acceptance criterion ("writing a new file with a matching import_pattern anchor surfaces the lesson") unmet for four of six supported languages.

Direct irony: sutra/280 replaced the hardcoded rust/dart literal in lessons.rs with an adapter-derived set while this identical hardcoded pair sat untouched, leaving the guard unable to produce imports for most of the languages the derived set now recognizes.

Note this also affects the pre-existing pattern-constraint and proposed-imports constraint paths, which share `parse_proposed` — widening it is a behavior change for those too, and should be checked deliberately rather than assumed safe.
